MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

I'm trying to submit a new package (tinyVAST) to CRAN, and getting what I think is a new CRAN check with note below (see attached for full copy of checks) that seems to be triggered by my integration of TMB.  I don't see anything about this note in the TMB materials online <https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/wiki/Development#distributing-code>, and actually don't see the subsection "Moving into C API compliance" in the R manual (although I see some chatter in R devel comments e.g. here <https://stat.ethz.ch/pipermail/r-devel/2024-June/083489.html>).

Has anyone seen this, or have a suggested fix?

Thanks
Jim

* checking compiled code ... NOTE
File 'tinyVAST/libs/x64/tinyVAST.dll':
  Found non-API call to R: 'ENCLOS'

Compiled code should not call non-API entry points in R.

See 'Writing portable packages' in the 'Writing R Extensions' manual,
and section 'Moving into C API compliance' for issues with the use of
non-API entry points.

